```java
public class GymMembership {
    private String name;
    private int visitsLeft;
    private int purchased;

    public GymMembership(String name, int visits) {
        this.name = name;
        visitsLeft = visits;
        purchased = 0;
    }

    public String getName() {
        return name;
    }

    public int getVisitsLeft() {
        return visitsLeft;
    }

    public boolean checkIn() {
        if (visitsLeft > 0) {
            visitsLeft--;
            return true;
        }
        return false;
    }

    public void addVisits(int n) {
        if (n > 0) {
            int before = purchased / 10;
            purchased += n;
            int after = purchased / 10;
            visitsLeft += n + (after - before);
        }
    }
}
```

The bonus counts how many new multiples of 10 the purchased total crosses: integer division gives the number of complete tens before and after the purchase. In the example, 6 / 10 = 0 and 11 / 10 = 1, so one bonus visit is added.
